# hk: Optimize external BO implicit sync under virtio
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44932 state=closed
# hk: Optimize external BO implicit sync under virtio

Under virtio, shared BOs are implicitly synchronized by the host on
every submit that carries them, chaining each job to the previous one
and preventing the kernel from keeping multiple jobs in flight.

Only submits that wait on or signal shareable syncs (e.g. WSI) need this
synchronization:
- Waiting submits only need the implicit fences of the BOs (READ).
- Signalling submits only need to publish their fence (WRITE).
- Looped submits only wrap the first (READ) and last (WRITE) ioctl.

For BOs imported from outside the driver (HK_EXTRES_FOREIGN), keep full
implicit sync unconditionally to preserve external synchronization
guarantees. An atomic counter (`foreign_count`) is used to completely
skip the sync iteration on internal submits when no foreign BOs exist.

Signed-off-by: s0ullight <opossum.pizazz-5h@icloud.com>
